    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras enter today\u2019s slate with a clear focus on speed and volume, headlined by **Pete Crow-Armstrong** (73.77) and **Yordan Alvarez** (72.97). **Pete Crow-Armstrong** is our premier play, benefiting from a soft matchup against Gausman and a highly favorable 90% SB probability driven by the pitcher's slow delivery. Simultaneously, **Yordan Alvarez** remains locked into the core, offering elite xwOBA potential and a strong platoon advantage against Bibee. We are also keeping a close eye on **Junior Caminero** (67.50); while his park factor is dampened, he draws a high-value start against Poulin, where his ability to capitalize on a 5.00 xERA outweighs the minor park-induced production loss.\n\nStrategic platoon alignments are bolstering the middle of our order today. **Josh Smith** (62.54) and **Lars Nootbaar** (61.48) both receive significant boosts from dynamic platoon adjustments, elevating them above their baseline projections. While **Christian Yelich** (59.62) faces a minor hit due to the L/L matchup against P\u00e9rez, his leadoff spot and situational consistency keep him firmly in the green. Our most difficult decision arrived at the 2B/MI slot, where **Colt Keith** (42.00) narrowly missed the cut. Despite his favorable wind conditions and the slow delivery of Eisert, his bottom-tier lineup positioning and poor platoon splits against a same-handed pitcher relegated him to the bench in favor of the more efficient **Casey Schmitt**. \n\nRisk mitigation remains a priority as we manage our game caps. Several starters, including **Gary Sanchez**, **Josh Smith**, **Christian Yelich**, **Yordan Alvarez**, **Nelson Velazquez**, and **Lars Nootbaar**, remain subject to official confirmation. Any significant shifts in their batting order could necessitate a late-cycle roster adjustment, particularly given the volatility inherent in our lower-floor utility spots. We are effectively playing a \"wait and see\" approach on the weather and lineup cards, but the analytical framework remains committed to maximizing our SB opportunities while protecting our lead in the core batting categories.",
